                <pb facs="0351" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg251"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.61383 J 41/36a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-24T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                                1920—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>23. News item appearing in local press January 22nd with Mexico City date line
                    quotes Sub-secretary of Foreign Relations as having announced the Jenkins’ case
                    satisfactorily settled. Investigate and report by telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
